Alembic migrations for the dispatch backend (landed v1.0.12).

env.py reads DATABASE_URL from the environment so the same migration
scripts apply to SQLite (local dev + Fly.io SQLite-on-volume) and Postgres
(future production scale-up). target_metadata = Base.metadata so
autogenerate diffs against the ORM definitions in models.py.

# Common commands (run from the repository root, with DATABASE_URL set):
#
#   alembic upgrade head                                  # apply all pending
#   alembic downgrade -1                                  # one step back
#   alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe_change"  # new migration
#   alembic current                                       # what's applied
#   alembic history                                       # full timeline
#   alembic stamp <revision>                              # mark applied w/o running

The canonical operator runbook is in ../DEPLOY.md § "5. Database migrations".
